(lang dune 3.16)
(context default)

; Keep the resolver off ocaml-compiler 5.5.0.
;
; 5.5.0's opam file uses the "build-id" variable, which no dune with a binary
; release understands yet. 3.21.0 is the newest binary release, so both CI and
; anyone who installed dune from ocaml-dune/dune-bin hit
;
;   File "packages/ocaml-compiler/ocaml-compiler.5.5.0/opam", line 1:
;   Error: Variable "build-id" is not supported.
;
; and "dune pkg lock" fails outright. That is what kept CI red from 2026-05-12
; onward: every run died in "Lock dependencies" and never reached build or
; test. Resolution picks 5.4.1 with or without this constraint; the constraint
; only stops 5.5.0 being considered in the first place.
;
; Drop this once a dune with a binary release can read 5.5.0's opam file.
(lock_dir
 (constraints (ocaml (< 5.5.0))))
